## Command Reference

### General Syntax
```bash
cryptocore [SUBCOMMAND] [OPTIONS]
```

### Encryption/Decryption Commands

#### **Encrypt**
```bash
cryptocore encrypt \
  --algorithm aes \
  --mode <mode> \
  [--key <hex-key>] \
  [--iv <hex-iv>] \
  [--aad <hex-aad>] \
  --input <input-file> \
  [--output <output-file>]
```

#### **Decrypt**
```bash
cryptocore decrypt \
  --algorithm aes \
  --mode <mode> \
  --key <hex-key> \
  [--iv <hex-iv>] \
  [--aad <hex-aad>] \
  --input <input-file> \
  [--output <output-file>]
```

### Hash/MAC Commands

#### **Hash**
```bash
cryptocore hash \
  --algorithm <sha256|sha3-256> \
  --input <input-file> \
  [--output <output-file>]
```

#### **MAC Generation**
```bash
cryptocore mac <hmac|cmac> \
  --key <hex-key> \
  --input <input-file> \
  [--output <output-file>]
```

#### **MAC Verification**
```bash
cryptocore mac <hmac|cmac> \
  --key <hex-key> \
  --input <input-file> \
  --verify <mac-file>
```

### Key Derivation Commands

#### **Derive Key**
```bash
cryptocore derive \
  [--password <text>] \
  [--password-file <file>] \
  [--password-env <env-var>] \
  [--salt <hex-salt>] \
  [--iterations <count>] \
  [--length <bytes>] \
  --algorithm pbkdf2 \
  [--output <output-file>]
```

